-- chem/he.cub — helium's ground state from above, exactly: the Ritz bound on Hylleraas functions as a generalized
-- eigenproblem with exact rational matrices, its lowest level bracketed by the inertia engine (chem/inertiaq.cub).
-- In atomic units H = −½∇₁² − ½∇₂² − 2/r₁ − 2/r₂ + 1/r₁₂. The basis (Hylleraas, Z. Phys. 54 (1929) 347): the singlet
-- S functions φ_ijk = (r₁^i r₂^j + r₁^j r₂^i) r₁₂^k e^{−α(r₁+r₂)}, i ≤ j, α = p/q rational, one exponent for all.
-- Every matrix element is a sum of the integrals K(a,b,c) = ∫∫ r₁^a r₂^b r₁₂^c e^{−β(r₁+r₂)} d³r₁ d³r₂, β = 2α,
-- with a, b, c ≥ −1. Over functions of r₁, r₂, r₁₂ alone, d³r₁ d³r₂ = 8π² r₁ r₂ r₁₂ dr₁ dr₂ dr₁₂ on the triangle
-- |r₁ − r₂| ≤ r₁₂ ≤ r₁ + r₂; in s = r₁ + r₂, t = r₁ − r₂, u = r₁₂ (dr₁ dr₂ dr₁₂ = ½ ds dt du, 0 ≤ |t| ≤ u ≤ s) the
-- integral factors: with A = a + 1, B = b + 1, C = c + 1 and c_m the coefficient of t^m in (1 + t)^A (1 − t)^B,
--   K(a,b,c)/(8π²) = J(A,B,C) = 2^{−(A+B)} (A+B+C+2)! / β^{A+B+C+3} · Σ_{m even ≤ A+B} c_m / ((m + 1)(C + m + 2)),
-- since ∫_{−u}^{u} t^m dt = 2u^{m+1}/(m+1) for m even, ∫_0^s u^{C+m+1} du = s^{C+m+2}/(C+m+2), and the power of s is
-- A + B + C + 2 for every m, ∫_0^∞ s^N e^{−βs} ds = N!/β^{N+1}: a rational in α (Claude's derivation; the s, t, u
-- reduction is Hylleraas's). The factor 8π² is common to every element and dropped. The kinetic energy in the
-- symmetric form ½∫(∇₁f·∇₁g + ∇₂f·∇₂g) (integration by parts), with f = r₁^i r₂^j r₁₂^k e^{−αs}: ∇₁f = (i/r₁ − α) f r̂₁
-- + (k/r₁₂) f ∇₁r₁₂, |∇₁r₁₂| = 1, r̂₁·∇₁r₁₂ = (r₁² + r₁₂² − r₂²)/(2 r₁ r₁₂); so for f, g with exponents (i,j,k), (i′,j′,k′)
-- and I = i + i′, J = j + j′, K = k + k′, ∇₁f·∇₁g is fg times
--   (i i′ + (ik′ + i′k)/2) r₁⁻² − α(i + i′ + (k + k′)/2) r₁⁻¹ + α² + (k k′ + (ik′ + i′k)/2) r₁₂⁻²
--   − ((ik′ + i′k)/2) r₁⁻² r₂² r₁₂⁻² − (α(k + k′)/2) r₁ r₁₂⁻² + (α(k + k′)/2) r₁⁻¹ r₂² r₁₂⁻²,
-- and ∇₂f·∇₂g the same with r₁ and r₂, i and j exchanged. Every power stays ≥ −1 wherever its coefficient is nonzero,
-- so every term is a K. Symmetrized functions: since H commutes with the exchange of the electrons,
-- ⟨φ_x|O|φ_y⟩ = 2(⟨m_x|O|m_y⟩ + ⟨m_x|O|m_ȳ⟩), m the monomial and ȳ the exponents with i and j exchanged; the 2 is
-- dropped. The theorem at each basis: the lowest level of H c = E S c lies in the computed interval [lo, hi], and by
-- Ritz (Cauchy interlacing) it is an upper bound to He's ground energy, −2.903724… hartree; that comparison with the
-- continuum operator is the open comparison step (docs/chemical-identity.md, "Notes, uncertainty first", (b)).
-- One function at α = 27/16 gives exactly −(27/16)² = −2.84765625, the textbook value.
import "inertiaq.cub"

